# Artifacts whose bytes are hashed into published evidence must not be renormalized
# per platform. A benchmark report records the SHA-256 of the protocol and policy it
# ran under, and the evidence builder recomputes those hashes from the working copy to
# refuse a drifted package. With autocrlf on Windows a fresh checkout produces CRLF and
# every hash changes, so an honest package becomes unpublishable on one platform and
# publishable on another. Pin them to LF so the hash is a property of the artifact.
benchmark/*.json text eol=lf
policies/**/*.json text eol=lf
policies/**/*.rego text eol=lf
